# Continuous Since (tests the "maintained continuously" semantics)
#
# "If relative_computed is true, then position_sent has been true
#  continuously since position_measured was true"
#
# In a single drone: phases go position_measured -> position_sent ->
# processing -> relative_computed, so position_sent does NOT hold
# continuously (processing breaks the chain).
# In multi-drone: other drones' propositions contribute to the global
# state, so the result depends on concurrency and linearization.
relative_computed -> (position_sent S position_measured)
